From: Keishi Hattori <keishi@google.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:36:56 -0700
Subject: PagePopup: Fix dangling WebPagePopupImpl::opener_web_view_

HTMLInputElement::showPicker() can open a popup for a disconnected or
display:none <input> element, including during pagehide or change events
inside WebViewImpl::Close(). Because Document::DetachLayoutTree() does
not visit disconnected or display:none elements, it does not close their
popups on document shutdown, and WebPagePopupImpl::opener_web_view_ can
dangle after WebViewImpl is destroyed.

This CL fixes the issue by:
* Closing any open popup owned by a detaching document in
  ChromeClientImpl::DocumentDetached(), and closing <input> pickers
  before cross-document adoption in Node::WillMoveToNewDocument().
* Clearing opener_web_view_ in WebViewImpl::CleanupPagePopup(),
  WebPagePopupImpl::ClosePopup(), and WebPagePopupImpl::Close() because
  WebPagePopupImpl stays alive until its Mojo channel disconnects.

Bug: 566377256
Change-Id: I89d02b41df709e65b815f224ce62d4df13ab2cbc
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8619575
Commit-Queue: Keishi Hattori <keishi@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Joey Arhar <jarhar@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Kent Tamura <tkent@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1725566}

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y): opener_web_view_ is a plain WebViewImpl*
on this branch, so the raw_ptr annotation hunk is dropped (the pointer is
still cleared through the new ClearOpenerWebView()); node.cc only gains the
html_input_element.h include from the conflicting include hunk.
internal_popup_menu_test.cc diverged too far to merge and keeps the branch
version (test-only). All other hunks apply as upstream.

